es avec la fonction `fviz_eig()`. \n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-19_189c9919f43ea4c4d2850cc3d7646451'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nrespca<-PCA(Ozone,quali.sup=c(11,12),scale.unit = F,graph=F)\nrespca$eig\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\n         eigenvalue percentage of variance cumulative percentage of variance\ncomp 1  825.6179071            94.54035814                          94.54036\ncomp 2   16.9181147             1.93726978                          96.47763\ncomp 3   16.2447331             1.86016179                          98.33779\ncomp 4    5.1530123             0.59006427                          98.92785\ncomp 5    3.0845093             0.35320287                          99.28106\ncomp 6    2.3463320             0.26867521                          99.54973\ncomp 7    1.3545802             0.15511110                          99.70484\ncomp 8    1.2006745             0.13748756                          99.84233\ncomp 9    0.9444947             0.10815278                          99.95048\ncomp 10   0.4324259             0.04951649                         100.00000\n```\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_eig(respca)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-19-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n### Etude des individus \n\n**Question :** Que contient la sortie `respca$ind$coord$` ? Comparez avec les résultats de la partie précédente ? Vérifiez visuellement à l'aide de la commande `fviz_pca_ind(respca)`.  \n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-20_c649ee1eb97ad6dc3632f191b99eabfd'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_ind(respca,geom=c(\"point\"))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-20-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n**Question :** Que représentent les graphiques suivants ? Commentez. \n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-21_d0dcbe6f1fd8e83fc4c131edc6119606'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_ind(respca,col.ind=\"contrib\",geom=c(\"point\"))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-21-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_ind(respca,geom=c(\"point\"),select.ind = list(cos2=0.95))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-21-2.png){width=672}\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_ind(respca,habillage=11,geom=c(\"point\"))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-21-3.png){width=672}\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_ind(respca,habillage=12,geom=c(\"point\"))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-21-4.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Etude des variables\n\n**Question :** On représente le graphique des corrélations entre les variables initiales et les méta-variables. Commentez.\n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-22_9c18a197e8ec455e6b9ed6ad34dc91a9'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nplot(respca,choix=\"varcor\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-22-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n**Question :** Afin de visualiser les corrélations des variables initiales avec toutes les méta-variables, utilisez la fonction `corrplot()`. Commentez. \n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-23_0c469a70241e7c931b0ca07beb8b7cd9'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ncorrplot(respca$var$cor,method=\"ellipse\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-23-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n# ACP centrée réduite\n\n## A la main \n\nOn fait maintenant une analyse en composantes principales sur les données centrées et réduites. \n \n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-24_82bd6cfa16bd2713880585a2fac3d2bd'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ns<-sqrt((n-1)*apply(OzoneC,2,var)/n)\nOzoneCR<-OzoneC%*%diag(1/s)\n```\n:::\n\n\n**Question :** Comparez `OzoneCR` avec `scale(Ozone[,-c(11,12)])`.\n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-25_40463b74fd30a2f34de8187c9153a584'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# A COMPLETER\n```\n:::\n\n\n:::{.callout-note custom-style=\"correction\" appearance=\"simple\" title=\"Correction\"}\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-26_57f60871cc458602f6233a583d54ffa7'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nhead(OzoneCR)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\n               [,1]       [,2]       [,3]        [,4]        [,5]         [,6]\n20010601 -0.1177278 -0.8880454 -0.7521395 -0.93727903 -0.35945082 -0.448069455\n20010602 -0.2959103 -0.4377041 -0.7769890 -1.09246948  0.02765006 -0.007860868\n20010603  0.0604548 -0.9845471 -0.9757846 -0.69340833 -1.13365259 -0.007860868\n20010604  0.8444581 -0.6950420 -0.4539462 -0.02830642 -1.52075347 -1.768695216\n20010605  0.1317278 -0.3090352 -0.2551506 -0.49387776  1.18895272  1.312764893\n20010606 -0.3671834 -0.2125335 -0.4290967 -0.95944910  0.41475095  0.432347719\n               [,7]       [,8]        [,9]      [,10]\n20010601  1.3651524  0.7283376 -0.03560567  0.3560461\n20010602  0.9344564 -1.1887825 -0.85837422 -0.4680103\n20010603 -0.3576315  1.5905399  1.25411341  0.7905219\n20010604 -2.0804153  0.8390602  0.70362487  0.5422755\n20010605  0.9344564  0.2725508 -0.48268673 -0.9434495\n20010606  0.9344564 -1.6878739 -1.21767749 -1.5403489\n```\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nhead(scale(Ozone[,-c(11,12)]))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\n               maxO3         T9        T12         T15         Ne9         Ne12\n20010601 -0.11720102 -0.8840720 -0.7487743 -0.93308537 -0.35784253 -0.446064660\n20010602 -0.29458634 -0.4357457 -0.7735125 -1.08758145  0.02752635 -0.007825696\n20010603  0.06018431 -0.9801419 -0.9714186 -0.69030582 -1.12858029 -0.007825696\n20010604  0.84067974 -0.6919321 -0.4519151 -0.02817977 -1.51394917 -1.760781551\n20010605  0.13113844 -0.3076525 -0.2540090 -0.49166800  1.18363299  1.306891196\n20010606 -0.36554047 -0.2115826 -0.4271768 -0.95515624  0.41289523  0.430413268\n               Ne15        Vx9        Vx12       Vx15\n20010601  1.3590443  0.7250788 -0.03544636  0.3544530\n20010602  0.9302754 -1.1834635 -0.85453360 -0.4659163\n20010603 -0.3560313  1.5834233  1.24850213  0.7869849\n20010604 -2.0711070  0.8353060  0.70047665  0.5398492\n20010605  0.9302754  0.2713314 -0.48052704 -0.9392282\n20010606  0.9302754 -1.6803219 -1.21222924 -1.5334569\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n:::\n\n**Question :** Quelle matrice cherche-t-on à diagonaliser dans ce cadre en ACP ?\nProgrammez cette matrice et diagonalisez-la à l'aide de la fonction `eigen()`.\n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-27_40a3f6fe99e7727594a83ef639046898'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# A COMPLETER\nGamma2<- .... \nB<-eigen(...)  \n```\n:::\n\n\n\n:::{.callout-note custom-style=\"correction\" appearance=\"simple\" title=\"Correction\"}\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-28_a60c98b60219f60b7780fb2b56dce361'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nGamma2<-t(OzoneCR)%*%W%*%OzoneCR  # (n-1)*cor(Ozone[,-c(11,12)])/n  \nB<-eigen(Gamma2%*%M)\n```\n:::\n\n:::\n\n**Question :** Que représentent les valeurs propres dans ce cas ? Que représente la somme de ces valeurs propres ? Vérifiez numériquement. \n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-29_09061a4a81606ae3827851b790036a32'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# A COMPLETER\n```\n:::\n\n\n:::{.callout-note custom-style=\"correction\" appearance=\"simple\" title=\"Correction\"}\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-30_b647403b6ac404d77d3bc319a25a78f3'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nB$values\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\n [1] 5.86849076 1.79480435 0.82289456 0.45006967 0.34767874 0.25343220\n [7] 0.18152187 0.15797033 0.09070360 0.03243391\n```\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nsum(B$values)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\n[1] 10\n```\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nInertie=sum(OzoneCR^2)/n\nInertie\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\n[1] 10\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n:::\n\n**Question :** Comment peut-on obtenir les résultats de cette ACP centrée réduite à partir du tableau de données centrées. Vérifiez numériquement. \n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-31_9e5775c1a231f56a60f976a698c9d230'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# A COMPLETER\n```\n:::\n\n\n:::{.callout-note custom-style=\"correction\" appearance=\"simple\" title=\"Correction\"}\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-32_8863fd454d278121abe0424891dc2945'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nV<-(n-1)*apply(OzoneC,2,var)/n\nM<-diag(1/V)\nGamma<-t(OzoneC)%*%W%*%OzoneC \neigen(Gamma%*%M)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\neigen() decomposition\n$values\n [1] 5.86849076 1.79480435 0.82289456 0.45006967 0.34767874 0.25343220\n [7] 0.18152187 0.15797033 0.09070360 0.03243391\n\n$vectors\n             [,1]        [,2]       [,3]        [,4]         [,5]         [,6]\n [1,]  0.95642601 -0.81076580 0.87339881  0.50953607 -0.967634299  0.997130434\n [2,]  0.09057083 -0.23766281 0.17884014  0.02989243  0.112446459 -0.014339376\n [3,]  0.13804051 -0.24987914 0.13912011 -0.06291551  0.008391432 -0.038088834\n [4,]  0.15739574 -0.25409553 0.08151976 -0.35701969  0.021206788 -0.036939839\n [5,] -0.08411793 -0.02863628 0.14059255 -0.58606889  0.006148810  0.011858894\n [6,] -0.07694030 -0.00521981 0.19455035 -0.16547786  0.028103447  0.014455722\n [7,] -0.06484141 -0.02387939 0.28064424  0.44726887 -0.031824336 -0.012777942\n [8,]  0.07391323  0.17572793 0.14132879 -0.18887309 -0.167119002 -0.038363925\n [9,]  0.07568279  0.24666644 0.09614871 -0.02816806  0.069248266 -0.007380799\n[10,]  0.06947315  0.25696094 0.11659828  0.02612345  0.126313222  0.025900277\n             [,7]        [,8]        [,9]       [,10]\n [1,] -0.53012703 -0.69040429 -0.26350889 -0.03583229\n [2,]  0.11118512 -0.21396827  0.53558586 -0.10642743\n [3,] -0.23565101  0.24099190 -0.24078949  0.72959735\n [4,]  0.15245955  0.16104126 -0.67364476 -0.65191688\n [5,] -0.46241598  0.04235049  0.08871324 -0.03953204\n [6,]  0.52879036 -0.07102240 -0.13799740  0.11996576\n [7,] -0.21865214  0.04919737 -0.07826496 -0.09710730\n [8,]  0.17200225  0.03002554  0.19983942 -0.01828170\n [9,] -0.23610300 -0.45472981 -0.22740392  0.05374461\n[10,]  0.03524128  0.42024904  0.08512903 -0.03839575\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n:::\n\n## Avec FactoMineR\n\n**Question :**\nOn fait une ACP centrée réduite à l'aide de la fonction `PCA()` de la librairie `FactoMineR` en imposant `scale.unit=T` et on trace  les valeurs propres à l'aide de `fviz_eig()` de la librairie `factoextra`. Interprétez les résultats. \n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-33_6db88fa06d28eb546137f8794e76d405'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nrespca2<-PCA(Ozone,quali.sup=c(11,12),scale.unit=T,graph=F)\nrespca2$eig\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\n        eigenvalue percentage of variance cumulative percentage of variance\ncomp 1  5.86849076             58.6849076                          58.68491\ncomp 2  1.79480435             17.9480435                          76.63295\ncomp 3  0.82289456              8.2289456                          84.86190\ncomp 4  0.45006967              4.5006967                          89.36259\ncomp 5  0.34767874              3.4767874                          92.83938\ncomp 6  0.25343220              2.5343220                          95.37370\ncomp 7  0.18152187              1.8152187                          97.18892\ncomp 8  0.15797033              1.5797033                          98.76862\ncomp 9  0.09070360              0.9070360                          99.67566\ncomp 10 0.03243391              0.3243391                         100.00000\n```\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_eig(respca2)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-33-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n**Question :** Représentez le graphe des individus et celui des variables à l'aide des fonctions `fviz_pca_ind()`et `fviz_pca_var()` dans le premier plan factoriel. Quelles différences remarquez-vous avec l'ACP centrée ? \n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-34_aaf4a9afe81680fd758c8d27ec0227ad'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# A COMPLETER\n```\n:::\n\n\n:::{.callout-note custom-style=\"correction\" appearance=\"simple\" title=\"Correction\"}\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-35_918cfc302b3fca4c71f1f38866164fd1'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_var(respca2)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-35-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_ind(respca2,geom=c(\"point\"))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-35-2.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n:::\n\n**Question :** Afin de visualiser les corrélations des variables intiales avec toutes les méta-variables, utilisez la fonction `corrplot()`. Commentez.\n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-36_f1a1beb0f2ed323c36bb4481e118d5af'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# A COMPLETER\n```\n:::\n\n\n:::{.callout-note custom-style=\"correction\" appearance=\"simple\" title=\"Correction\"}\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-37_ab047f724be4b68c3a4362a05683ba1f'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ncorrplot(respca2$var$cor,method=\"ellipse\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-37-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n:::\n\n**Question :** Poursuivez l'exploitation des résultats en regardant d'autres plans factoriels, en exploitant l'information des variables qualitatives **pluie** et **vent**. \n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-38_a90b621f8e96e0b7af2e8ba187b8b5fe'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# A COMPLETER\n```\n:::\n\n\n:::{.callout-note custom-style=\"correction\" appearance=\"simple\" title=\"Correction\"}\n\n- Composantes principales / variables initiales :\n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-39_f5c22743977aeb183a32cce1c1ada91b'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_var(respca2,axes=c(1,2))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-39-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_var(respca2,axes=c(1,3))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-39-2.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n- Contributions des variables à la construction des axes principaux :\n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-40_f75b07728592b063774bdd5ae791d44c'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_contrib(respca2,choice=\"var\",axes = 1)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-40-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_contrib(respca2,choice=\"var\",axes = 2)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-40-2.png){width=672}\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_contrib(respca2,choice=\"var\",axes = 3)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-40-3.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n- Projection des individus dans les plans factoriels :\n\n  + Couleur en fonction du vent\n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-41_f4c9cd92fbd2268cd80524ddc2ab12df'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_ind(respca2,habillage=11,axes=c(1,2),label=\"none\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-41-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_ind(respca2,habillage=11,axes=c(1,3),label=\"none\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-41-2.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n  + Couleur en fonction de la pluie\n\n\n::: {.cell hash='2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_cache/html/unnamed-chunk-42_a09cddbc10917eee7978321da1c1eb74'}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_ind(respca2,habillage=12,axes=c(1,2),label=\"none\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-42-1.png){width=672}\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfviz_pca_ind(respca2,habillage=12,axes=c(1,3),label=\"none\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](2526-TP3-ACP-Correction_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-42-2.png){width=672}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\n\n",
